# The build context for every def is the REPO ROOT (defs/*/build.sh pass
# "$SCRIPT_DIR/../.."), because variant Dockerfiles resolve their COPY paths from
# there. Without this file the daemon received the whole tree — 303 MB, of which
# 201 MB is node_modules and 83 MB is apps/ — on every single image build, and
# defs/base/Dockerfile's builder stage baked it into a layer with `COPY . .`.
#
# defs/cecli/.dockerignore is NOT this file and never applied: BuildKit reads
# <context>/.dockerignore or <dockerfile>.dockerignore, and that path is neither.
#
# This is a denylist on purpose. An allowlist (`*` + `!`) would be tighter, but
# five Dockerfiles COPY from this context — AGENTS.md, cmd/, internal/, go.mod,
# go.sum, defs/**, packages/lib/** — and a new COPY silently reaching nothing is a
# worse failure than a slightly wide context.

# JS toolchain: never copied by any Dockerfile, and the bulk of the context.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# The CLI's web assets — built and published by wrangler, not by any image.
apps

# VCS. Nothing in a build reads it; `go build` simply skips VCS stamping.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# Local test/build output.
cov
dist
*.out
*.log
.DS_Store

# Agent- and editor-local state.
.claude
.vscode
.idea
